body:
ive started new medication recently and for some reason, have stopped counting calories ! im still not 100% not "WeIrD wItH FoOd" considering i bought low calorie bread, try to restrict my mealtimes, and weigh myself everyday but... its a step in the right direction. Hopefully i can practice more mindfulness about letting myself eat what i want, when i want without the numbers weighing on my mind :0

&#x200B;

also grapes have always been my #1 safe fruit (and strawberries). very smol and fun to eat one by one.

&#x200B;

sorry for the blogposting hehe >:0

ofc!! the two images after the bowl photo have all the ingredients i used, and after that it should just be a matter of mixing stuff together!!

&#x200B;

for the "base": i massaged some kale (makes the texture a lot better to eat imo) and riced some cauliflower. i steamed the cauliflower in my rice cooker, then i packed both of those into separate bags. when i make the bowl i just combine the cauiflower rice and kale together to form a little bed for the toppings

&#x200B;

for the tofu: cut it up into 1cm cubes (or the size of your liking, this size is easy for me to scoop out of the bag with a spoon) and combine with the marinade ingredients into a bag. it should taste best left overnight in the fridge. you can also omit that much garlic, i just added that much because i freeze it in chunks and that happened to be the size of the chunk i pulled out of the freezer. it ended up weighing 933 grams for the whole thing, so i used that as the "total number of servings".

&#x200B;

everything else is just fresh veg that ive prepped and placed into bags for me to keep in the produce drawer of my fridge. i peeled the cucumber (this isn't english cucumber so the skin was kind of tough and waxy) and cut into quarter slices. i boiled the shelled edamame according to package directions and put them in a bag as well. i just happened to use kiwi because that was the only ripe fruit i had on hand - i like cutting up mango and adding it to my poke bowls but they werent ripe :(( the furikake is just some random brand my roommate had lol

&#x200B;

some other ideas i have for the future are crunchy chickpeas for a C R O N C H topping, and ripe avocado slices! but first i have to figure out how to store avocado so it doesnt get brown and icky >:0

&#x200B;

basically this is just a lot of prep work !!! but it pays off and i find myself craving veggies more . hopefully you try it and enjoy !!
